 format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIZUKA, TOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OIE, NAOKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TABATA, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An operation control method for an air conditioning system for preventing the concurrent restarting of a plurality of air conditioning systems that may cause the re-stopping of the systems due to a drop in voltage at the time of an automatic restoration when the power is restored, and an air conditioning system. The air conditioning system is provided with an automatic restoration control circuit (21) that determines a delay time up to restarting in accordance with a setting data for determining the operation of the air conditioning system the circuit belongs to and restarts the own air conditioning system based on the determined delay time.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne, d'une part, un procédé de commande pour système de climatisation qui empêche le redémarrage concurrent de plusieurs systèmes de climatisation qui risque de provoquer un arrêt des systèmes dû à une chute de tension lorsque l'alimentation est automatiquement rétablie et, d'autre part, un système de climatisation. Le système de climatisation est pourvu d'un circuit (21) de commande de rétablissement automatique de l'alimentation qui, d'une part, détermine un temps de retard précédant le redémarrage conformément aux données de réglage, et ce pour déterminer le fonctionnement du système de climatisation auquel appartient le circuit et, d'autre part, redémarre son propre système de climatisation sur la base du temps de retard déterminé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>